<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0026> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> "'May be triggered' is the language of a factor, and Part 29.6 then names the question the examiner must ultimately decide separately from it. The well-known person is the material; the connotation of endorsement is what is decided."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0026> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/conceptGroup> "relevant_factor" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0026> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/confidence> "0.75"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0026> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> "How much of the well-known-person branch this record carries. Three of the factors at 29.6 — how well known, name commonness, closeness of the field — have no concept of their own, so they are currently unmodelled and this record is standing in for them."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
