<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0046> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> "GC-0046's own record flags that holding \"the Registrar's delegate\" as an alt label is probably wrong, because a delegate exercises the power and is not the Registrar. Correcting that narrows the concept; it stays a process_role either way. Whether examiner, decision maker and Registrar are three roles or three names used loosely for one. GC-0044, GC-0045 and GC-0046 hold them apart on the concept records, all three are typed process_role here, and this typing inherits the question rather than answering it."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
