<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0051> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> "Kept in none_of_these deliberately, and the only one of the 53 that stays. The concept is a statement about how a provision operates — that section 43 applies mandatorily and there is no discretion to accept a mark caught by it. That is not a ground, a test, a factor or an exception; and it is not a role, a thing, a step, a record or an external scheme. It is a rule *about* a ground, and nine groups have no place for one."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0051> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/conceptGroup> "none_of_these" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0051> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/confidence> "0.6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GT-0051> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> "Whether the vocabulary should carry modality statements as concepts at all, or whether 'the application of section 43 is mandatory' is a property of the section 43 ground rather than a concept standing beside it. GC-0051's own record says this concept and GC-0007 pull in opposite directions, and that tension is still unresolved — GT-0007 is typed exception and this one is typed nothing."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
