<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0058> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> "Subsection 41(1) states the ground and subsection 41(2) makes 'taken not to be capable of distinguishing' depend on 41(3) or 41(4). The concept is therefore the top of a small structure the Manual works through in order, and it is held separately from inherent adaptation for that reason."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
