<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0072> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Manual makes the point that matters most here: the definition of trade mark is closed and exhaustive, while the definition of sign is open and inclusive. A sign is a trade mark only when used or intended to be used to distinguish in the course of trade."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
