<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0130> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> "The evidence is the defensive-registration requirement, which is reputation described rather than named. Held because reputation is one of the few concepts that genuinely spans the Manual — Parts 29, 34, 46 and 47 all reason with it — and the boundary removal is what makes that visible. Overlaps the signed GC-0050."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0130> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/confidence> "0.6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0130> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/definitionSource> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0130> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> "Whether reputation under section 43, section 60 and section 185 is one concept or three. This is the most consequential unresolved question in the pass."@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0130> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/goldRecord> "GC-0130" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
