<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/scheme-s43> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Australian trade marks examination vocabulary"@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/approved> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/scheme-s43> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Australian trade marks examination vocabulary"@en-AU <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/authored> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An assertion a named human approved on a date. The only kind that may sit in the approved named graph (CLAUDE.md rule 4)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Approved assertion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedRelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A predicate on the closed list in `relations.ttl` **that a named expert used in\na record they signed**.\n\nExtraction may only propose relationships from the closed list. An open\npredicate set makes precision unmeasurable — with no fixed vocabulary, a wrong\npredicate and a new one are the same event, so nothing can be scored\n(ontology/README.md).\n\nMembership has not changed and is not expected to: the fourteen terms here come\nfrom the 35 signed relationships, every one of which is sourced to TMM/Part29.\nA fifteenth arrives when an expert approves a relationship that uses one."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Approved relation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This project's record that something was extracted from a passage, by some method, and reviewed by someone. Not the proposition itself — the act of asserting it, with everything an audit needs."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assertion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An assertion a machine wrote and no expert has validated (ADR-0079, ADR-0080).\n\nDeliberately NOT a subclass of tmk:ApprovedAssertion and deliberately not in the approved named graph. It is the same shape as one — same subject, predicate, object, passage, span and hash — and differs in exactly the fact that matters: nobody signed it. A query written against tmk:ApprovedAssertion therefore cannot pick one of these up by accident, which is the whole point of giving it its own class rather than a flag.\n\nIt carries tmk:reviewStatus \"unreviewed\" and never \"approved\": approval moves a record to eval/gold/ through tmk-transcribe, and a record that has moved is rebuilt as a tmk:ApprovedAssertion on the next build (ADR-0086)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authored assertion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredRelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A predicate on the closed list that **a machine used and no expert has read**.\n\nAdded 2026-09-12 (ADR-0109). Until then the closed list was generated from the\nsigned register alone, which was correct while an agent could not author a\nrelationship at all — and which left the dictionary a section 43 dictionary for\nfour days after ADR-0081 withdrew the boundary. Nothing in the fourteen\napproved terms can say that a concept is *defined by* a provision, that a step\nis *performed by* an office, or that one *must occur within* a period, and\nthose are most of what the Manual's other 53 Parts state.\n\nA class rather than a flag, for ADR-0007's reason: a flag can be dropped by a\ncareless projection and a class has to be asked for. A predicate both stores\nuse carries both types, and the two usage counters beside it are never added —\n`tmk:usageCount` keeps its meaning as the signed count so that nothing reading\nit starts silently including unreviewed records (ADR-0080 consequence 3).\n\n**A term being here is not evidence the relation it names is real.** It is\nevidence that a deterministic pass found sentences stating it and committed to\na reading, with the evidence and the doubt recorded on every record\n(`authored/relationships.yaml`)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthoredRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authored relation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Something that can be cited in support of a proposition. Legislation, a decision, or the Registrar's own practice material — all three, and the point of the module is that they are not interchangeable."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authority"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether an authority is current, superseded or repealed."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authority status"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CandidateAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CandidateAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. Machine output awaiting a human. Kept in the candidates named graph and never in the approved one; if the two mix once, no later audit can unmix them (ADR-0007)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CandidateAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Candidate assertion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CandidateAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One retrievable passage of the Manual — the addressable unit of this repo, keyed by `chunk_ref`."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manual chunk"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One reference from a passage to an authority, reified so that upstream's\ntrust metadata survives (CLAUDE.md rule 3).\n\nA bare triple `chunk -> provision` throws away the two things that separate an\nauthor's assertion from a machine's inference, and once thrown away they cannot\nbe recovered from the graph. So the edge is a node: it carries how it was found\nand how certain that was, and `tmk:citesProvision` exists beside it only as a\nconvenience for queries that genuinely do not care."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Citation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CompetencyQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CompetencyQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A question the finished system must be able to answer. If a question has no query and no query has a question, one of the two is wrong (queries/README.md)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/CompetencyQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Competency question"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ConceptScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ConceptScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge concept scheme"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ConceptScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Current> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Current> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "current"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DecisionMaker> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DecisionMaker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED — HANDOFF Q17, and the reviewer corrected two records on precisely\nthis point (GE-0010, GE-0047: decision maker vs the Registrar).\n\nIt matters for Q16: the office's bar for applying the presumption of\nregistrability is not that the individual examiner doubts a connotation exists,\nbut that the Registrar as a whole does. A model that equates the two roles\nloses that distinction silently."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DecisionMaker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Decision maker"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DecisionMaker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Delegate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Delegate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED — HANDOFF Q17. The word exists in the vocabulary only inside GC-0046's alt label «the Registrar's delegate», which is not the same as holding the term: nothing can say that a delegate decided something."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Delegate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delegate"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Delegate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Document> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A source document: the Manual, an Act, a set of Regulations. Identified independently of any particular capture of it."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DocumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DocumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One capture of a Document. In this repo a version is the pinned upstream\nsnapshot: an extractor version and a commit sha, recorded in `data/pin.json`.\n\nThere is no corpus-level month stamp. The roadmap's `2026-01` form implies one\nand none exists (Q-05); the amendment history is the upstream repository's git\nhistory and is not held here."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DocumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document version"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One occurrence of a term in a passage, at an offset. Two mentions of the same words in the same chunk are two records (GE-0005 and GE-0006), because recall is measured over occurrences."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entity mention"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. Material put before the decision maker."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. A kind of evidence, as the practice material groups them."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence category"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInAnswer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInAnswer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED · AUTHORED, unreviewed. The applicant's evidence, filed in answer to evidence in support. No expert has read this declaration."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInAnswer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence in answer"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInAnswer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInReply> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInReply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED · AUTHORED, unreviewed. The opponent's evidence in reply, which closes the sequence. No expert has read this declaration."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInReply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence in reply"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInReply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInSupport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInSupport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED · AUTHORED, unreviewed. The opponent's evidence, filed first. Named in terms across the opposition Parts; no expert has read this declaration."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInSupport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence in support"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceInSupport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. The act of filing evidence in a matter."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidenceSubmission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidence submission"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidentiaryProposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidentiaryProposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED, and it must stay unpopulated while automated reasoning is bounded\nas it is.\n\n'The evidence establishes acquired distinctiveness' is an evaluative conclusion\nand stays outside automated reasoning scope (queries/README.md). A class that\nholds such propositions is fine; a rule that derives one is not."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidentiaryProposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evidentiary proposition"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EvidentiaryProposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalProposition>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. The process applied to an application."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Examination"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExaminationOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExaminationOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED, and it must stay that way for this pilot.\n\nDeciding an examination outcome is explicitly out of scope (CLAUDE.md §6), and\nthe prohibited-use set exists to keep it there: PU-0001 and PU-0002 are the two\noutputs that state one."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExaminationOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Examination outcome"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examiner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examiner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED as a class. GC-0044 carries the term and 7 of the 31 authored isPerformedBy edges name it as the office that takes a step — the Registrar takes 13 of the rest, the applicant 9. Every one of them is unreviewed, and the applicant's 9 are the ones to distrust: an applicant more often has a step done to them than does one."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examiner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Examiner"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Examiner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Exception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Exception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else — never from a label or a heuristic. In the approved graph that record is one a named expert signed; in the authored graph it is one a machine wrote and nobody has read, and the two never share a graph (ADR-0080). A condition under which a general position does not hold, or is reversed."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Exception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Exception"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Exception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExternalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExternalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else. A treaty or international scheme Australian practice adopts, rather than a rule the Act itself makes.\n\nSmall, and it earns its place on the honesty argument rather than the size one:\nCLAUDE.md rule 5 turns on keeping the source of an obligation visible, and a\nretrieval surface that cannot tell the Madrid Protocol from a section of the Act\nhas lost exactly the distinction the rule protects."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExternalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "External instrument"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ExternalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/GroundOfRefusal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/GroundOfRefusal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else — never from a label or a heuristic. In the approved graph that record is one a named expert signed; in the authored graph it is one a machine wrote and nobody has read, and the two never share a graph (ADR-0080). A statutory basis on which registration may be refused."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/GroundOfRefusal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ground of refusal"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/GroundOfRefusal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Guidance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Guidance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Non-binding material that is neither legislation nor a decision. Declared for the roadmap's model; nothing in the approved set is classified into it yet."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Guidance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Guidance"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Guidance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InferredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InferredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Produced by an approved CONSTRUCT rule, never authored. Must identify its source facts and the rule that produced it: an inference that cannot explain itself does not get published."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InferredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inferred assertion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InferredAssertion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InstrumentOrRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InstrumentOrRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else. A document, entry or endorsement the process produces, or writes to the Register. The Register itself is here, as are the things entered on it — a disclaimer, an endorsement, conditions or limitations — and the documents that start or end a proceeding."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InstrumentOrRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Instrument or record"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InstrumentOrRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A decided case. **Citation level only.** No decision text exists anywhere in\nthis programme (Q-11, HANDOFF Q6), so a decision node carries a citation, party\nnames where the Manual gives them, and the Manual's own account of it — never\nthe reasons. 'Which cases interpret this test' is answerable; 'what did the\ncourt hold' is not, and PU-0005 is the output that pretends otherwise."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Judicial decision"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concept in the examination vocabulary, with a preferred label, its variants, and — crucially — the labels it must not be confused with."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal concept"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Anything an approved relation may hold between: a concept, a provision, a\nManual passage, a decision.\n\nIt exists because the approved relationships do not agree on narrower types.\n`requiresElement` runs Provision→Concept twice, Concept→Concept three times and\nConcept→Provision once; `excludesBasis` runs both ways. Asserting a narrow\n`rdfs:domain` on that evidence would, under OWL RL, silently reclassify every\nsubject of the property — a careless range assertion manufactures\nclassifications (ontology/README.md).\n\nSo the asserted domain and range are this union superclass, which licenses only\n'this is a legal matter', and the narrow types each predicate has actually been\nseen with are recorded as annotations that infer nothing. Tightening them is an\nexpert ruling, and `tmk-ontology-report` lists the candidates."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal matter"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalProposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalProposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A statement that something is so, held together with the passage that states\nit and the authority of that passage.\n\nDistinct from tmk:Assertion, which is this repo's record *that* a proposition\nwas extracted and approved. The proposition is what the corpus says; the\nassertion is what this project did about it."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalProposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal proposition"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalTest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else — never from a label or a heuristic. In the approved graph that record is one a named expert signed; in the authored graph it is one a machine wrote and nobody has read, and the two never share a graph (ADR-0080). A question the decision maker must answer, with a stated threshold."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legal test"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Legislation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Legislation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An instrument. This corpus holds two: the Trade Marks Act 1995 and the Trade Marks Regulations 1995."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Legislation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legislation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Legislation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Document>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A section, regulation, Schedule clause or container of an instrument, keyed by its provision ref. It is law."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legislative provision"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A numbered unit inside a provision — subsection, paragraph, definition.\n\nModelled as a subclass rather than as a sibling because a ref does not say what\nlevel it addresses: 228 legislation refs in the pinned corpus cannot be placed\nby grammar alone (Q-18, ADR-0025). Anything true of a provision is true of a\nunit of one, so the subclass licenses nothing the corpus cannot support."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Legislative unit"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A statement of the Registrar's practice, sourced from the Manual.\n\nIt is **not law**. It does not bind the Registrar's discretion. A system that\nlets a Manual instruction be read as a statutory requirement has committed the\nerror PU-0004 names, and that error is a live one in this corpus: the Manual\nquotes s 43 in full inside TMM/Part29/1#1, so an answer can appear to cite the\nAct while having read only the Manual (CQ-0001's caveat)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manual instruction"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ManualInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/NotHeld> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/NotHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cited by the corpus and held nowhere in the programme.\n\nNot a defect and not a gap to be filled by guessing: s 114 of the *Trade Marks\nAct 1905* is cited by Part 29.3.1, the instrument is not in this corpus, and it\ncan be neither excluded (the Manual relies on it) nor resolved (Q-24). 17\ndistinct refs cited from the in-scope chunks are in this state, and CQ-0020 asks\nfor exactly this list."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/NotHeld> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "not held"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Objection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Objection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. A ground raised against an application in an examination."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Objection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Objection"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One page of the Manual, as crawled. Holds everything constant across the chunks cut from it."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manual page"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Anything in the corpus that bears text at a stable address and carries a content hash. The superclass of everything a citation can point at."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Passage"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProceduralStep> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProceduralStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else. An act, proceeding or event that moves an application or a registration from one state to the next.\n\nDeliberately wider than \"something somebody does\": lapsing is in this class and\nnobody performs it. What the class holds is a transition, whether it is\nperformed, ordered or merely suffered — which is why the modality of each step\nis a property of the concept and not of the group."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProceduralStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Procedural step"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProceduralStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProcessRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProcessRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else. A person or body that acts under the Act — the concept of the office, as the vocabulary holds it.\n\nNOT tmk:Role, and the distinction is load-bearing. A tmk:Role in the examination\nmodule is somebody who acts: an examiner who signs a report. A tmk:ProcessRole\nis the *term* \"examiner\" as an entry in the vocabulary. Merging them would make\nthe concept record for examiner an examiner, and the model would lose its only\nway of saying which of the two it is talking about."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProcessRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Process role"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProcessRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProcessRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProhibitedUse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProhibitedUse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An output the system must never produce, with the reason.\n\nThe roadmap requires examples of conclusions the system must NOT draw, and they\nare as important as the positive ones. Six kinds: evaluative_conclusion,\nauthority_conflation, unsupported_inference, overreach, ambiguity_collapse and\nstale_source."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProhibitedUse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Prohibited use"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ReasoningExpectation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ReasoningExpectation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What a correct system should conclude from a stated set of facts, and what it must not."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ReasoningExpectation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reasoning expectation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ReasoningExpectation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Registrar> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Registrar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED as a class, but the vocabulary now carries the term twice — GC-0046 signed, GC-0115 authored — and that duplication is one of the ten ADR-0101 put to the expert rather than something to tidy away. Load-bearing here: the Manual states practice and does not bind this office's discretion."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Registrar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Registrar"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Registrar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevanceJudgement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevanceJudgement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Relevance judgement"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevantFactor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevantFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else — never from a label or a heuristic. In the approved graph that record is one a named expert signed; in the authored graph it is one a machine wrote and nobody has read, and the two never share a graph (ADR-0080). Something the decision maker weighs, which does not on its own decide the question."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevantFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Relevant factor"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RelevantFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RetrievalQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RetrievalQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A question with the evidence a correct answer must rest on, and the conclusions it must not reach."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RetrievalQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AI retrieval question"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A person or office acting in the examination system."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Role"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SearchQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SearchQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A query with graded relevance judgements, and — the valuable half — the passages that are tempting and wrong."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SearchQuestion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Search question"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filled from a concept-types.yaml record and from nothing else. The thing the process operates on — what may be registered, and the kinds of sign and registration the Act holds apart. A sign, a shape trade mark, a certification trade mark and a protected international trade mark are all subject matter; what refuses, tests or excepts them is not."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Subject matter"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatterExpert> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatterExpert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED, and the term is ABSENT FROM BOTH STORES — one of the four of the reviewer's nine that the whole-Manual concept pass still did not reach (Q-53). The expert request asks for it in prose rather than guessing at a record."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatterExpert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Subject matter expert"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SubjectMatterExpert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Superseded> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Superseded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Every superseded instruction has a status date' — one of the six starting SHACL rules."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Superseded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "superseded"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TeamLeader> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TeamLeader> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNDEFINED, and ABSENT FROM BOTH STORES. Named in the reviewer's note as part of the consultation the office expects before a connotation is accepted on the basis of doubt (Q16), and the Manual names a «Examination team leader» in Part 38 — so the corpus has the words and the vocabulary has not taken them."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TeamLeader> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Team leader"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TeamLeader> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Role>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TradeMarkApplication> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TradeMarkApplication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNPOPULATED. The thing being examined. No application data exists in this programme and none is in scope."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/TradeMarkApplication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trade mark application"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedRelation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Approved usage: 1 relationship (GR-0006), sourced to TMM/Part29."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "allocates to"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/allocatesTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsageCount> "0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>  .
