<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "assertion subject"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The authority a proposition is being *presented as coming from*.\n\nSeparate from tmk:statedIn, which is where the words are, and the separation is\nthe whole point. PU-0004 — \"Section 43 of the Act requires the connotation to be\nobvious, direct and immediate\" — is a proposition stated in a Manual passage and\nattributed to the Act. Every word of it is in the corpus and the attribution is\nwrong, which is why it is worth a constraint rather than a test: a shape blocks\npublication, a test only reports (shapes/README.md).\n\n`shapes/authority.ttl` fails any proposition stated in a practice passage and\nattributed to a legislative provision."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalProposition>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attributed to"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The model that wrote this, with its version. Never a person's name — a person's name goes in tmk:approvedBy and only a transcription from a signed workbook puts it there (ADR-0087)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authored by"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredDate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredDate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredDate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authored date"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredDate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsageCount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsageCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "How many authored relationships use this predicate. Beside tmk:usageCount and never summed with it: one counts records a person signed and the other counts records nobody has read, and a single figure would answer the only question that matters — how much of this has been looked at — in the wrong direction (ADR-0080 c3)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsageCount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authored usage count"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The authored record ids that use this predicate, truncated past a dozen because the route back to the sentences is only useful while it is short. The full set is in `authored/relationships.yaml`, which is the register; this is the index."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoredUsedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authored used by"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringBasis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What the judgement rests on: \"corpus_explicit\" — the corpus states it in terms; \"corpus_inferred\" — the corpus supports it but the reading is the machine's; \"general_knowledge\" — the corpus does not say it. The third is permitted and flagged, never hidden: an unevidenced assertion is not thereby wrong, it is thereby unevidenced, and no count may present it as equivalent to an evidenced one (ADR-0079 guard 2)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authoring basis"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Why this reading and not the obvious alternative, written for the expert who will disagree with it. The field that makes correction cheap, which is the entire premise of ADR-0079."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authoring reasoning"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authoringReasoning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What kind of thing is speaking, and with what force.\n\nThis is the module CLAUDE.md rule 5 lives in. The Manual states the Registrar's\npractice; it does not bind the Registrar's discretion and it is not legislation.\nThe distinction is carried here as a class disjointness rather than as a flag,\nbecause a flag can be dropped by a projection and a disjointness cannot be\nsatisfied by an assertion that ignores it."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — authority module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/document>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True where an answer must keep the Act and the Manual visibly apart.\n\nThis is CLAUDE.md rule 5 expressed as a per-question requirement, and it is the\nflag `shapes/authority.ttl` reads: a question carrying it whose required\nevidence is entirely Manual passages is a question whose correct answer must say\nso in words, because nothing in the sources will say it for them."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/RetrievalQuestion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authority distinction required"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityDistinctionRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`law` | `practice` | `decision`. Redundant with the class, on purpose: it is\nwhat a retrieval projection carries when it has dropped the types, and it is\nwhat a shape checks when it wants to catch a projection that dropped them\nsilently. A SPARQL result that names a passage without this is missing the one\nfact CLAUDE.md rule 5 requires it to carry."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authority kind"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authority status"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/AuthorityStatus>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedAt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When upstream captured the passage. The nearest thing this corpus has to a currency date, and it is a capture time, not an in-force date."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "captured at"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedAt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The snapshot version this passage was read from. Every Passage carries one — 'every source passage identifies a document version' is one of the six starting SHACL rules."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "captured in"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DocumentVersion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caseCitation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caseCitation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caseCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/JudicialDecision>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caseCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "case citation"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caseCitation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caveat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caveat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "caveat"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/caveat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`explicit` | `default` | `ambiguous`, present on `regex` edges only.\n\n`default` is upstream's inference from a bare 'section 43' — an inference, not a\nstatement by IP Australia. `ambiguous` is upstream refusing to choose between\ninstruments, and it is never resolved here: an ambiguous edge is a reason to put\na passage in front of a person, never a reason to drop it (Q-07)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "certainty"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`body`, `annex` or `landing`. Kept because the corpus is lopsided — 725 of its\n2,460 chunks are annex material — and retrieval that treats every chunk alike\nsurfaces a great deal of it (Q-10)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chunk kind"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Whether the cited ref lands on something this corpus holds. False is a fact about the corpus, not a defect in the citation — s 114 of the 1905 Act is cited by Part 29.3.1 and is held nowhere in the programme (Q-24)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "citation resolves"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/citationResolves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean>  .
