<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concept layer, and the module with the largest declared-but-unpopulated\npart of the model.\n\nEvery approved concept in `eval/gold/concepts.yaml` becomes a `tmk:LegalConcept`.\nWhether it is also one of the four subclasses below — GroundOfRefusal, LegalTest,\nRelevantFactor, Exception — depends on a signed record in\n`eval/gold/concept-types.yaml`, and on nothing else. Deciding that 'connotation'\nis a LegalTest rather than a RelevantFactor is a legal judgement this repo may\nnot make (CLAUDE.md rule 1); what it may do is hold the answer somebody gives.\n\nThe owner confirmed the four groups on 2026-09-08 (OQ-0001) and the container\nnow exists (ADR-0071). Until a concept has a type record it stays a bare\n`tmk:LegalConcept`, and the count of unsorted concepts is reported by every\nbuild rather than defaulted away. A machine filling these would produce a\ntaxonomy that reads as authoritative and was authored by nobody."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — legal concepts module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The provision the concept operates under. A concept can have a legislative basis and still be a creature of practice — the basis says which ground it belongs to, not that the Act uses the word."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "legislative basis"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision>  .
