<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ADR-0011's field list as RDF, over PROV-O.\n\nThe rule this module exists to make enforceable: an assertion that cannot say\nwhere it came from does not get published. Every approved relationship in the\ngraph appears twice — once as a direct triple so SPARQL is natural, and once as\na tmk:Assertion carrying the passage, the span, the hash, the reviewer and the\ndate. A SHACL shape fails if the first exists without the second (ADR-0058).\n\nThe field list is deliberately open (ADR-0041): Stage 2 has not run, so what a\nmachine-generated candidate needs to carry is not yet known from evidence. What\nis here is what the approved records actually carry today."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — provenance module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/document>  .
