<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supersedesRejected> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supersedesRejected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The id of a record a named expert rejected, where this authored assertion covers the same ground. A signed rejection is a human decision and ADR-0079 does not license reversing one silently: naming it, with the difference explained in tmk:authoringReasoning, is the only way an authored record may occupy that ground (ADR-0084 consequence 2)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supersedesRejected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supersedesRejected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supersedes rejected record"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supersedesRejected> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingSource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supporting source"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingText> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The sentence that states it, verbatim. Checked against the snapshot at the recorded offsets: if the text at the span is not this string, the record is stale or the surface was retyped rather than copied (ADR-0045)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "supporting text"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/supportingText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/surface> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "surface"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/temptingButIrrelevant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/temptingButIrrelevant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A passage a naive matcher will surface and that is wrong. The most valuable field on a search record — it is what separates a retrieval score from a retrieval result."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/temptingButIrrelevant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/SearchQuestion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/temptingButIrrelevant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tempting but irrelevant"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/temptingButIrrelevant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/testsBoundaryOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/testsBoundaryOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concept whose not-label explains the boundary. The edge exists so the pairing can be read back: this question tests the edge of that concept, and here is the signed record that drew the edge."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/testsBoundaryOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tests boundary of"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/testsBoundaryOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The passage's text exactly as upstream emitted it. Never normalised here — spans are offsets into this string."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Passage>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "text"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "1 deterministic · 2 low-risk · 3 legally significant (ADR-0008). An expert's call; the ontology only knows there are three."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tier"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/tier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dates, currency and what this corpus cannot answer about time.\n\nThe honest headline: **point-in-time questions are out of the pilot scope draft\nand the snapshot cannot support them.** There is no corpus-level version stamp\n(Q-05); the amendment history is the upstream repository's git history, and\nanswering 'what guidance was current on «date»' properly needs a full-history\nclone, which is a different data strategy rather than a different query. CQ-0014\nis marked out of scope on the strength of that line.\n\nWhat the module does carry is the currency mechanism that actually works:\nstaleness by content hash. An assertion whose source hash no longer matches the\npin is stale and returns to review. That is Stage 10's whole incremental\nmechanism and it needs no version stamp."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — time module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/typedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/typedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The record that put this concept in one of the nine groups.\n\nPresent so a typed concept can be traced to whoever or whatever typed it and the\ndate they did, rather than appearing to have always been a LegalTest. The nine\nclasses are the one place in this model where a class membership is a judgement\nrather than a structural fact, so the judgement carries its provenance — and\nsince ADR-0079 that provenance is load-bearing rather than merely tidy, because\nthe typing may have been written by a model no expert has read.\n\nFollow it and read what you find: the assertion node carries tmk:origin and\ntmk:reviewStatus, and a concept whose only typing is authored has been sorted by\nnobody."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/typedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/typedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "typed by"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamCommit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamCommit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamCommit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The pinned `manual-XtrACTor` commit sha. This, plus the extractor versions, is what makes a rebuild reproducible."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamCommit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/DocumentVersion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamCommit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "upstream commit"@en-AU  .
