<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s181(2)> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "(2) In addition to its powers under Division 2 of Part 8 in relation to certification trade marks, a prescribed court may, on the application of a person aggrieved, order that the Register be rectified by cancelling the registration of a certification trade mark, or removing or amending an entry in the Register relating to the certification trade mark, on the ground that:" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
