<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "An application for the registration of a trade mark in respect of particular goods or services must be rejected if, because of some connotation that the trade mark or a sign contained in the trade mark has, the use of the trade mark in relation to those goods or services would be likely to deceive or cause confusion." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
