<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7(1)> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "(1) If the Registrar or a prescribed court, having regard to the circumstances of a particular case, thinks fit, the Registrar or the court may decide that a person has used a trade mark if it is established that the person has used the trade mark with additions or alterations that do not substantially affect the identity of the trade mark." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
