<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s79~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If, within 6 months after the registration of a trade mark has expired, a person asks the Registrar, in accordance with subsection 75(2), to renew the registration of the trade mark, the Registrar must renew the registration of the trade mark for 10 years from the day on which the registration expired." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
