<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "1.1.9 Trusts -" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "10.1. Formality requirements - Name" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 10 Details of Formality Requirements" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part10" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Where the name of an applicant appears to be the name of a trust, this should be queried. The trust’s name as applicant should be replaced by the name(s) of the trustee(s). A trust imposes a personal equitable obligation on the trustee to deal with the property for the benefit of the beneficiaries or for the advancement of certain purposes (e.g. a charity). Because a trust is a relationship, not an entity with legal personality, it cannot be an applicant or registered owner of a trade mark in its own right. It is the trustee or trustees who should be specified as the applicant. The trustee will be bound by its common law and equitable duties, as well as the terms of the trust deed, to deal with the property of the trust (including any trade marks) appropriately. The trustees may in the application reference the fact they are applying in their capacity as trustees, e.g. John Smith as trustee for the Smith Family Trust. However, reference to the existence of a trust in the application form is not compulsory." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part10/1/1/1/9" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
