<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part10" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "In most cases the applicant will need to file a copy of the actual sound being claimed as the trade mark. This copy should be provided on a medium which allows for easy copying, storage and replaying of the sound. CDs, DVDs and digital sound files are all suitable media. If it is not possible to provide the actual sound at the time of filing, for example, when the applicant experiences difficulties in attaching a sound file to an electronically filed application, the medium incorporating the sound should be sent to the Office as soon as possible after the application is filed." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part10/3/3/3/4" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
