<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/6/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The applicant should state on their application whether the sign they are claiming as a trade mark is a moving image, hologram or gesture. These applications will be indexed according to their content. For example, a moving image which consists of a three dimensional animal performing certain actions will be indexed as “shape” as well as the description of the animal. A moving image which consists of a two dimensional animal performing actions will not be indexed as a shape but as the animal only." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
