<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/3/3/7/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If the applicant is claiming a taste or flavour as a trade mark, an actual example will not be required. As with scent trade marks, the applicant will need to provide a clear description that identifies the taste in terms which are easily understood by the average buyer, and which describe how the taste is to be used as a trade mark. Part 21 Non-traditional signs - 10. Other kinds of non-traditional signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
