<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 12 Divisional Applications" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part12" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Division 3 of Part 4 of the Act sets out a process whereby a trade mark applicant may file an application (divisional application) as a limited continuation of their current application (parent application) under certain circumstances. Divisional applications claim the priority date of the original parent application, however, they receive a new trade mark number and must meet the conditions specified in sections 45 and 46 of the Act." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part12/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part12/1#1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
