<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part13/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Mark Regulations 1995 Under section 51 of the Act, a person may make a single application for a series of two or more trade marks if: the trade marks resemble each other in material particulars and the trade marks differ only in respect of one or more of the following: (a) statements or representations as to the goods or services in relation to which the trade marks are to be used; (b) statements or representations as to number, price, quality or names of places; (c) the colour of any part of the trade mark. This may be referred to as a “series application”. If the application succeeds, the trade marks shall be registered as a series in a single registration." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
