<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/1%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part14" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/1%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The Trade Marks Classification Search allows you to search a database of goods and services that you can choose for your trade mark, sorted into classes. This database is called ‘the picklist’. All terms in the database have been deemed by both IP Australia and the World Intellectual Property Organisation (WIPO) to be acceptable for use in trade mark applications and correctly classified. Using only terms from this database will allow trade mark applicants to avoid classification issues being raised by IP Australia. The database also includes a snapshot of the types of goods and services that fall in each class ('class headings'), as well as more detailed information explaining what falls into each class and why. This information will assist trade mark applicants whose goods or services are not covered by an existing term in the picklist to determine the appropriate class. https://tmgns.search.ipaustralia.gov.au/" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
