<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/4/4/10/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "29"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/4/4/10/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part14" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/4/4/10/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If, however, an application was filed in class 36 for insurance services when the applicant in fact sold computers to insurance agents, a transfer to class 35 to cover computer retailing services would not be possible as the original claim for insurance services could not be interpreted as having included these other specific services, being retailing services. The amendment would not be allowed under section 65." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/4/4/10/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part14/4/4/10/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
