<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 14 Classification of Goods and Services" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part14" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "These terms, used on their own in a specification, are considered to be too vague, and expressions such as “goods in this class” or “services in this class” are not acceptable. If used in conjunction with a description that adequately describes the type of goods or services, they will however be acceptable, for example: Class 16: Stationery goods." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
