<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2/prov/0> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "14.6. Wording of the specification" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "6.3 Registered trade marks are not to be used in specifications" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "6.3.2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 14 Classification of Goods and Services" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part14" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Examiners should familiarise themselves with the list in Annex A3 and if these, or other, trade marks appear in a specification, the applicant should be requested to delete them and provide a generic description of the goods or services, along the lines of the alternative descriptions given in Annex 3. For example, WINDCHEATER would not be acceptable in a class 25 specification where the applicant intends to cover close fitting garments for wind protection. WALKMAN would not be acceptable in a class 9 specification to cover portable audio equipment. Any amendment to the specification must not have the effect of extending the goods or services claimed as this is not allowed under section 65." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part14/6/6/3/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
