<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/3/3/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "In cases where the matter is not clear cut, the Registrar may require the person to make application in writing for the extension of time, supported by a declaration setting out the circumstances of the case. Reg 21.33 empowers the Registrar to ask for any documents not otherwise required by the Act or Regulations that are necessary to the proceedings." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
