<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> "body" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:3fc2bb1e2183e1603dc35d6cb30bba2264208b30123259405e55e0999aa50681" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "15.6. Extensions of time of more than three months" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "6.4 Where there is opposition to the extension of time" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 15 General Provision for Extensions of Time" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part15" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If opposition is filed to the application for extension of time, the procedures for filing evidence and providing for the parties to be heard are determined by the Registrar (see above). The determination of whether the extension is allowable will be made in the course of the opposition proceedings. There will not be any preliminary determination as to whether the time sought is appropriate, or is justified by the supporting declaration. If substantive justification for the extension only appears during the proceedings (as per evidence in answer), this may be reflected in the award of costs." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/6/6/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part15/6/6/4" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
