<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/2%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/2%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part16" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/2%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Mark Regulations 1995 Many responses to examiner's reports are filed close to or at the end of the period allowed. The practice to be followed in these circumstances is set out below. Under reg 4.10 the Registrar must consider the response and either accept the application or issue an adverse report in writing. The report must include the lapsing date." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/2%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part16/2#1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
