<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/4/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/4/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part17" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/4/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "4.1.1 If an application for deferment has been made on the ground that a pending application has been cited against the application and that citation has the same filing date as the application for which the request for deferral has been made, that request will be denied. • Part 26 Conflict with other Signs - Section 44 - 7. Trade marks with the same priority/filing date 4.1.2 If 4.1.1 does not apply, the citations are checked to make sure that at least one citation is a pending application. If this is the case, the deferment is entered on the system. 4.1.3 Where deferment has been requested for the purpose of gathering evidence to prove “prior use”, “honest concurrent use” or “other circumstances”, the examiner’s report is checked to ensure that a section 44 ground for rejection has been raised." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/4/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part17/4/4/1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
