<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:55dcf8a262492a2bba3fe8038cdca15a284aaf097d37325812c325b1fdbb2036" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "3.1 When to consider rejection of an application" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "3.2 Notification of intention to reject an application" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 18 Finalisation of Application for Registration" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 18.3. Rejection of an application for registration" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part18" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If the examiner is satisfied that the examination process has reached an impasse, the next step is to draft a Notice of Intention to Reject. The notice is in the form of a letter rather than a report. A proposal to reject an application should be issued by a delegate at the APS 6 level or above, after appropriate consultation The Notice of Intention to Reject will contain: a restatement of the ground(s) for rejection; reasons why submissions to date have not been sufficient to overcome those grounds; and all possible solutions to finalise acceptance of the application, including the options of requesting a hearing or the withdrawal of the application. A full review of the examination process will take place and all grounds for rejection will be re-assessed before dispatch of the Notice of Intention to Reject." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part18/3/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part18/3/3/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
