<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:bbb448dfa5dc6eb0abb00c9f61a31096c1992d37d2c0b960e0c6e00f43b122b1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3/prov/0> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3/prov/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "19B.4. The right to take infringement action" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.3 Infringement of trade mark by breach of certain restrictions" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 19B Rights Given by Registration of a Trade Mark" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part19B" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/4/4/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Under section 121 a registered trade mark is infringed if the registered owner, or an authorised user of the trade mark having power to do so, has caused to be displayed on goods in respect of which the trade mark is registered a notice of prohibition, and a person who acquires the goods does or authorises an act, in the course of trade, that is prohibited. Acts that are prohibited are set out in subsection 121(2). The trade mark is not infringed if the person acquired the goods in good faith and without being aware of the notice of prohibition or became the owner of the goods by virtue of a title derived from a person who had so acquired them." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
