<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "20.4. Presumption of registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 20 Definition of a Trade Mark and Presumption of Registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "It is clear from both the Oregon and Sports Warehouse decisions (as well as from other decisions from the Courts) that once the Registrar is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that a ground for rejection does exist, then the presumption of registrability no longer forms a part of the Registrar’s decision making process." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/4#1~2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
