<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> "practice" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/snapshot-c490a9927f1a> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> "body" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:556acd898f6bd382d069d4d1ab2a59d2744e445adb6100a1d3c8fcfda71b2996" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "20.4. Presumption of registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 20 Definition of a Trade Mark and Presumption of Registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If the Registrar or their delegate is satisfied that a ground (or grounds) for rejection does exist, then the presumption of registrability no longer applies. The ground or grounds upon which rejection is based must be articulated in a specific and supported manner, and documented in line with administrative requirements." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4/4/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/4/4/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
