<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part20/5%231/prov/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "20.5. Grounds for rejection and the presumption of registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 20 Definition of a Trade Mark and Presumption of Registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The Act and Regulations contain all the grounds upon which an application for registration of a trade mark may have to be rejected. Rejection may result under paragraph 33(1)(b) because of the question of registrability of the trade mark itself, or under paragraph 33(1)(a) from an application not being made in accordance with the Act, the latter including a failure to comply with formality requirements. If an application has been made in accordance with the Act, the trade mark is registrable provided none of the grounds referred to in sections 39 to 44 of the Act are found to apply. Sections 39 to 43 cover what are sometimes referred to as the “absolute” grounds for rejection, that is grounds which relate to the nature of the trade mark itself. Section 44 covers the grounds which might exist because of conflict with other registered trade marks, or trade marks which are the subjects of pending applications. These are referred to as the “relative” grounds for rejection." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/5#1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
