<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Where the Registrar or their delegate is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the trade mark has insufficient inherent adaptation to distinguish for it to be considered prima facie capable of distinguishing, the reasons for that decision must be clearly stated and documented. If there is a doubt that a ground for rejection exists, then the Registrar or their delegate is not satisfied and the ground for rejection should not be raised." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/5/5/3/1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
