<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 20 Definition of a Trade Mark and Presumption of Registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A trade mark must be rejected if the trade mark is not capable of distinguishing the applicant’s designated goods and/or services from the goods and/or services of other persons. The matters to be considered under section 41, in determining whether a trade mark is capable of distinguishing the applicant’s goods and/or services, are dealt with in detail in Part 22 of this manual." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/5/5/3" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
