<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:7cbf6c69b31fc08ddbd66b589334a4f7f8fa6eba22a6badedda36d75e0591276" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part20/5/5/5/prov/0> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "20.5. Grounds for rejection and the presumption of registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "5.5 Section 43 - Trade marks likely to deceive or cause confusion" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 20 Definition of a Trade Mark and Presumption of Registrability" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Under section 43 of the Act an application for registration of a trade mark for particular goods or services must be rejected if, because of some connotation that the trade mark has, the use of the trade mark in relation to those goods would be likely to deceive or cause confusion. The connotation may result from the whole trade mark or a sign included in it. Grounds for rejection under this section are “absolute” grounds in that the likely deception or confusion results from the nature of the trade mark. Section 43 does not apply to instances of deception and confusion that might arise from conflict between similar trade marks." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/5/5/5" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
