<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Section 44 deals with the “relative” grounds for rejection which must be considered as part of the examination of a trade mark application. These are the grounds which result from the existence of conflicting trade marks of earlier priority date." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
