<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:c0f238c4f9393257b20c7f5ebdda9995d9de67f96b73a2a25ea9e344b7f0089d" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "22.14. New terminology and \"fashionable\" words" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 22 Section 41 - Capable of Distinguishing" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part22" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Language and its usage are constantly changing. There are many words used today which were not in vogue or did not even exist five years ago, or which have changed their meaning with the passage of time. Examiners should take this into account when assessing the registrability of trade marks and should try to be aware of emerging trends in the use of language. For example, market interest in environmental issues has been characterised by use of words such as \"Green\" and \"Ozone\", and abbreviations such as \"Enviro\" and \"Eco\". The popularity of new words or phrases is not restricted to the environment. Many areas including modern technology, the Internet, and fashion develop new language and new uses of existing language which quickly become generic." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/14%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part22/14#1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
