<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/4/4/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/4/4/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part26" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/4/4/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Generally, custom manufacturers provide a point to point interaction with customers that involves both the goods and the services related to them. In cases where there is a sufficient degree of similarity between trade marks claiming a good and the custom manufacture of that good, a ground for rejection is likely to be appropriate." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
