<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/6/6/1~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part26" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/6/6/1~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "...the opponents case...must fail because, in relation to the goods in question here, I regard the visual impact of the marks, which is very different, to be of more importance than any aural similarity. The commercial reality today is that articles of clothing are simply not purchased over the counter on a verbal request but are carefully selected by a potential customer from a rack in a shop and very carefully inspected and compared with similar articles" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
