<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "8.2 Full assignments of applications and all assignments of registered trade marks" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 26 Section 44 and Regulation 4.15A - Conflict with Other Signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part26" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/8/8/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If, during the course of examination an examiner becomes aware that a registered trade mark, or an application for registration of a trade mark, that was previously in the name of the applicant (and therefore not a citation) has been assigned to a different person then a citation should be raised. This situation, however, would not normally be identified after the Registrar has completed the initial examination as required by s 31 of the Act. It is not required that all applications be re-examined before acceptance to identify such occurrences, although the examiner should raise an appropriate objection if a citation is brought to their attention prior to acceptance." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
