<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> "practice" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/capturedIn> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/snapshot-c490a9927f1a> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/chunkKind> "body" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:d9409929d056f9b10f7979753c0f0ff8332d7b7667f0e0320b5ebf03f942c113" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "27.4. Negotiation with owner/s of conflicting trade mark/s" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.2 Letters of consent" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.2.6" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 27 Overcoming Grounds for Rejection under Section 44" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part27" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "As an alternative to a letter of consent, the applicant may choose to supply a copy of an agreement between the two parties. Such an agreement will only be acceptable if it includes the information required for a letter of consent and does not include any conditions on use of the trade mark. Redacted agreements may be accepted provided that any redactions do not raise doubt regarding the scope of any consent provided by one party to the other in the agreement. For example, if parts of the agreement specifically dealing with the consent are redacted, this may indicate that consent is conditional and therefore not sufficient for acceptance by the Registrar. An explanation of the reasons for the redaction and confirmation that the redactions do not relate to conditions of use may be sufficient for the agreement to be accepted." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part27/4/4/2/6" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
