<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "The distinctiveness of the trade mark" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part28" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If the trade mark is a descriptive term or image or contains a descriptive term or image as its essential feature, purchasers are less likely to expect exclusive proprietorship. In Jean Patou Parfumeur v Crisena Corp Pty Ltd [1991] AIPC 90-388 Assistant Registrar Farquhar said that it was not surprising that more than one trader had selected the trade mark ‘Joy’. Expectations are likely to be different if the trade mark has a high degree of adaptation to distinguish." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part28/3/the-distinctiveness-of-the-trade-mark" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
