<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A connotation must arise from the trade mark itself, and not through a comparison with another trade mark. Such comparisons are dealt with under the provisions of section 44 of the Act, and discussed in detail in Part 26 of this Manual. Part 26 – Conflict with Other Signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
