<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The presumption of registrability applies to section 43. The Registrar must be satisfied that a ground for rejection exists before section 33(3) can be applied to reject the trade mark. If there is doubt that a connotation exists, then the ground for rejection should not be raised." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
