<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part29" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Where business identifiers are included in a trade mark (e.g. A TASMANIAN COMPANY, RIVERINA DAIRY CO.) this tends to indicate a characteristic of a business rather than the goods or services themselves. A ground for rejection will rarely apply in these cases. See USA Detergents, INC v Magnatex International Pty Limited [2001] ATMO 29; Deyncourt Pty Ltd v Scott Mitchell Passmore as trustee for The S R G Passmore Investment Trust [2019] ATMO 26." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
