<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part31" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Subsection 39(1) states that the Registrar must reject an application if the trade mark contains or consists of a sign that, under regulations made for the purposes of section 18, is not to be used as a trade mark. There are currently no regulations made for the purposes of section 18, which means grounds for rejection under s 39(1) are not raised during examination." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
