<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part31/3%231~1/prov/0> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "31.3. When does a ground for rejection exist under subsection 39(2)?" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 31 Prescribed and Prohibited Signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part31" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Subsection 39(2) is expressed in discretionary terms, stating that the Registrar ‘may’ (not ‘must’) raise a ground for rejection. The circumstances the Registrar must consider in exercising the discretion are not listed. However, it is in the public interest that signs are not used in a way that may give rise to a real, tangible danger of confusion amongst the public that there exists a state of affairs or connection that does not in fact exist. As such, and taking into account the presumption of registrability, a ground for rejection will generally only be appropriate under subsection 39(2) if a trade mark contains or consists of one or more of the signs prescribed and the presence of that sign would be likely to confuse the relevant public as to whether: the goods and services bearing the trade mark have a particular status given by legislation, or there is a connection between the applicant and the person, body, or organisation with whom the sign is associated. For example, presence of the prescribed sign may cause a member of the public to wonder whether a trade mark or the goods upon which the trade mark appears is patented or is subject to copyright protection. It could also suggest a false connection between the user of the trade mark and a particular organisation, person or governing body. That connection might include a direct implication of trade origin, sponsorship, patronage, permission or approval of the goods or services in respect of which the trade mark is used. In practice, a ground for rejection will be raised if the Registrar is satisfied that use of a trade mark containing or consisting of a prescribed sign would give rise to a likelihood of confusion. However, the Registrar can also consider raising grounds for rejection in other circumstances where it may be appropriate to do so. 3.1 In considering whether the public would be confused the following factors should be considered:" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part31/3#1~1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/3%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authorityKind> "practice" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
