<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.2.3 Commonwealth of Australia: floral and faunal emblems and official colours" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 31 Prescribed and Prohibited Signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part31" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Australia’s national floral emblem is the golden wattle (Acacia pycnantha Benth). When in flower, the golden wattle displays the national colours, green and gold. Further information can be found here. Permission is not required to reproduce the national floral emblem. No objection arises under section 39 for the use of the floral or faunal emblem or the national colours (green and gold). Any trade marks incorporating these features will be subject to the normal examination required for any trade mark application." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
