<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "31.4. Practice for examining trade marks containing the signs specified in reg 4.15" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.4 Article 6ter signs - Subreg 4.15(da) and (e)" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "4.4.4" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 31 Prescribed and Prohibited Signs" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part31" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Information to assist examiners in determining the scope of the protection has been entered into RIO. This information will indicate the nation, governmental organisation or intergovernmental organisation that the sign is being protected on behalf of, and the contact details of the relevant authority. For signs with limited protection, examiners should conduct research into the organisation’s activities (such as capturing information from the organisation’s website) to help determine if a section 39(2) ground for rejection should be raised. Examiners should also consider whether relevant organisation or authority still exists, and if not, when it ceased to operate. The fact that an organisation or authority may be defunct or may operate under a different name is one factor to consider in whether it is appropriate to raise grounds for rejection, but is not determinative in itself. Relevant factors may include the length of time since the organisation was active, its function, and its likely reputation amongst the Australian public. Consultation with QPC may be appropriate where a sign relates to a defunct organisation or authority." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part31/4/4/4/4" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
