<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/2/3/2-3-1-b-synonyms> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/2/3/2-3-1-b-synonyms> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part32A" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/2/3/2-3-1-b-synonyms> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "In the context of plant nomenclature, synonym has particular meaning. A synonym listed on the Register of Plant Varieties is recognised as an official name and is subject to the same considerations as a variety name. A name that does not appear as a synonym on a PBR Register (in Australia or overseas), but is used in the same way as a synonym in the market place, is known as an alternate name." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
