<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "2.3.3 Descriptive words which are common to the trade" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "32B.2.3 Section 41: Capacity to Distinguish" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 32B Examination of Trade Marks for Wines (in Class 33)" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part32B" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The wine industry has many terms which are in common use and add very little if any inherent adaptation to distinguish the trade marks in which they are used. Some of them are also protected terms (e.g. VINTAGE is a QWT). Examples of such words common to the trade are: ESTATE WINES BLEND CELLARS BIN WINERY VINEYARD VINTAGE RANGE" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part32B/2/3/2/3/3" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
