<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/4/2/4/1~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/4/2/4/1~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part32B" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/2/4/2/4/1~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "With regards to trade marks consisting of a Class 33 certification mark (CTM) such as Tequila or Scotch Whiskey, a s 44 objection should be raised where there is a real, tangible danger of consumer confusion between the CTM and the subject mark, not merely because the CTM is contained within." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
