<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part33" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Federal Register of Legislation - Trade Marks Regulations 1995 Federal Register of Legislation - Trade Marks Act 1995 A collective trade mark is a sign used or intended to be used, in relation to goods or services dealt with or provided in the course of trade by members of an association to distinguish those goods or services from goods or services so dealt with or provided by persons who are not members of the association. Unlike certification trade marks, the use of collective trade marks is not required to be subject to rules." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part33/1#1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
