<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "34.5. Grounds for rejection under Division 2 of Part 4 of the Act" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "5.2 Section 43" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 34 Defensive Trade Marks" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part34" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A trade mark subject of an application for defensive registration may have a connotation in respect of the goods specified in that application which it did not have in respect of the goods covered by the registration upon which it is based. Therefore, the possibility of the existence of grounds for rejection under section 43 must be considered. Part 29 Section 43 - Trade Marks likely to Deceive or Cause Confusion" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part34/5/5/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
