<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:23b1d51e534594973ac0d5ff4ba4670ea5eba988848e0815fd064cd0f37aef33" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "1.2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "38.1. What is revocation of acceptance?" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 38 Revocation of Acceptance" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part38" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Once an application has been revoked it no longer carries the status “Accepted” and re-enters the examination stream with the status “Under Examination”. At this stage the owner will typically be granted a free 15 month extension of time within which to overcome objections." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
