<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/1%231~3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/1%231~3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part43" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/1%231~3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "1.11 An unregistered certification trade mark which is the subject of an application that has already been sent to the ACCC under section 174 may only be assigned with the consent of the ACCC. The Registrar will not record details of a transfer of ownership unless the applicant provides evidence of the ACCC's consent (section 180A and reg 16.10A). For more information see the following parts: Part 33 Collective Trade Marks - 5. Assignment or transmission of collective trade marks Part 35 Certification Trade Marks - 8. Assignment of registered certification trade marks 9. Assignment of unregistered certification trade marks" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/1%231~3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part43/1#1~3" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
