<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/6/6/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part43" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/6/6/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "If, at step 4.4 of the normal assignment process, the application for assignment (which may be partial assignment) is found to relate to a registered certification trade mark, it should be accompanied by evidence of consent to the transfer of ownership by the ACCC. (The owner of a registered certification trade mark should first seek permission from the ACCC before assigning the trade mark to another person.) (Regs 10.1 and 16.11.) If consent has not been filed, details of the assignment should be captured but not recommended for approval. The applicant for recordal of the assignment should be advised that no further action will be taken until evidence of consent from the ACCC has been provided. If consent has been filed, then the assignment may proceed as normal. Part 35 Certification Trade Marks - 8. Assignment of registered certification trade marks" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
