<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part47" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Any person may oppose registration / protection of a trade mark by filing a notice of intention to oppose within two months from the day on which acceptance of the trade mark application was published (regs 5.6(1), 17A.33(1)). If the notice of intention to oppose was filed late and an application for an extension of time has not been received/granted (regs 5.9, 17A.34C), the notice of intention to oppose will be deemed not receivable. The parties will be informed of the reason why the notice is not receivable and the relevant fee will be refunded. If the notice of intention to oppose is filed before the trade mark application has been published as accepted, the notice will be deemed not receivable and the fee will be refunded." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part47/1/1/1/1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
