<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part47" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "This provision is equivalent to paragraph 131(1)(a) of the 1955 Act and the scope of that provision was considered in Atomic Skifabrik Alois Rohrmoser v. Registrar of Trade Marks [1987] FCA 22. This case should provide guidance on interpretation of \"circumstances beyond the control of the person concerned\". This force majeure provision encompasses circumstances which neither the person nor their agent could prevent, such as wars and terrorism, arson and vandalism, or forces of nature such as storms, earthquakes and floods." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
