<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 49.2. Opposition to non-use application" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part49" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The notice of intention to oppose must be filed in an approved form. Part 4 Fees A notice of intention to oppose form is available on IP Australia’s website. It is not a requirement that this form be used however it is a useful guide to ensure the notice of intention to oppose is filed in an approved form. If the potential opponent is the holder of the protected international trade mark which is the subject of the non-use application, it must also provide an address for service in Australia or New Zealand at the same time that it files the notice of intention to oppose." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part49/2/2/1/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
