<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/2/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A statement of grounds and particulars must be filed by the potential opponent within one month from the day the notice of intention to oppose is filed. If the statement of grounds and particulars has not been filed within the time allowed and no application has been made to extend the time (regs 9.11, 17A.48L), he statement will be returned to the potential opponent with the advice that as a complete notice of opposition has not been filed, removal of the trade mark may proceed." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
