<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/2/2/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "An adequate statement of grounds and particulars will typically contain brief facts about: the alleged use, or intended use, or circumstances preventing use, of the trade mark, or any other information that may justify the exercise of the Registrar's discretion not to remove the trade mark." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
