<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/10%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/10> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/10%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/10%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part51" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/10%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "O&H to email the TM details/issue to MDB-TMRevocation@ipaustralia.gov.au, the relevant section Team Leaders, and Quality, Practice and Customers (QP&C). Revocation of acceptance is considered by the Revocation Panel. Panel communicates recommendation to QP&C. If QP&C agrees with the panel recommendation the matter is progressed accordingly. If QP&C does not agree with the panel recommendation the matter is escalated to the QP&C AGM and the section AGM who will make a joint final determination on the matter. If the status of the TM shows that it is under opposition or if it has incoming correspondence on file relating to opposition proceedings, then the Team Leader must also email tmhearings@ipaustralia.gov.au informing them of any revocation of acceptance." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
