<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "1Under section 205 of the Act, a Deputy Registrar has all the powers and functions of the Registrar (except the power of delegation) and when a Deputy Registrar exercises a power or function under the Act, it is taken to have been exercised by the Registrar. Therefore, decisions issued by the Deputy Registrar are headed \"Decision of the Registrar of Trade Marks, with Reasons\" rather than “Decision of a delegate of the Registrar of Trade marks” (emphasis added)." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
