<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "5.6 Filing a Notice of Appeal at the Federal Court" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 52 Hearings, Decisions, Reasons and Appeals" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 52.5. Rights of appeal from decisions of the Registrar" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part52" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Rule 1.61(5) of the Federal Court Rules makes provision for the exclusion of a period of time in any given year from 24 December to 14 January of the following year in respect to the calculation of time. Unless otherwise varied by way of an order from the Federal Court, a delegate of the Registrar (who issues a decision) and officers in the Hearings Support Team, (who give effect to that decision) are to have regard to the provisions of Rule 1.61(5) of the Federal Court Rules 2011 to avoid the premature finalisation of a decision that: has an appeal period which falls in part or completely within the time specified in Rule 1.61(5) of the Federal Court Rules 2011 and is appellable to the Federal Court under Parts 33 or 34 of the Federal Court Rules. Similarly the timeframe for compliance by: the appellant under Rule 34.24 of the Federal Court Rules 2011 concerning service of the Notice of Appeal on the Registrar (and respondent(s) to the appeal) and the Registrar of Trade Marks under Rule 34.31 of the Federal Court Rules 2011 concerning the filing of documents (or certified copies of documents) in the appropriate Court Registry and written advice to the parties to the appeal should also been taken into account by the Deputy Registrar in Oppositions and Hearings during this period of time." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/5/5/6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part52/5/5/6" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
