<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "1.1 Expedited examination - applicant's request" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "6.1. Expedited Examination" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 6 Expedited Examination" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part6" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part6/1/1/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Applicants may make a request to the Registrar to expedite the examination of their application (reg 4.18). 1.1.1 A request for expedited examination must be made by the person who has applied for registration of the trade mark or their appointed agent. The request must be in writing (reg 4.18(1)(a)) and be accompanied by a declaration stating the reasons for the request (reg 4.18(1)(b)). The requirements for declarations are set out in reg 21.6. 1.1.2 The applicant must give reasons for the request and the Registrar will grant a request for expedited examination if the request is based upon reasonable grounds. The Registrar has the discretion to grant or refuse to grant such a request. Examples of reasons given in some instances where expedited examination has been granted are: the applicant being in real fear that their trade mark is being infringed or may be infringed; the applicant has invested in advertising and/or manufacture and requires registration of their trade mark at the earliest date possible so as to put their investment at as little risk as possible; the applicant wishes to file overseas." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
