<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/4/11/4/11/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part60" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/4/11/4/11/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Deferment is possible on request by the applicant if: a conflicting trade mark is pending, or the holder has taken non-use action under section 92 or Part 17A, Subdivision D of the Regulations against a conflicting trade mark; or a conflicting trade mark is not renewed but is still within the 6 month grace period; or the holder has begun proceedings to have the Register or the Record of international registrations rectified in respect of the conflicting trade mark; or the holder is seeking to establish honest concurrent use, prior use or other circumstances." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/4/11/4/11/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part60/4/11/4/11/3" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
