<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part61/6/6/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part61/6/6/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part61" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part61/6/6/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Section 217A requires the Registrar to make available for public inspection, documents that relate to a trade mark whilst held in the office or after the time particulars of the application for registration is published under section 30. As a TM Headstart is not a trade mark application and is not published under section 30 until the Part 2 fee has been paid any documents that are not part of the published application will not be made available for public inspection." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
