<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r16.2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:56315443b31fc13a7912bc5fe03d1a4065d6e6ba4b19696cf72c9f88d8894e9f" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r16.2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "(1) If, after examining an application, the Registrar is satisfied that: (a) the application has been made in accordance with this Act; and (b) there are no grounds for rejecting it; the Registrar must send to the Commission copies of the documents mentioned in subregulation (2). (2) For subregulation (1), the documents are: (a) the application for registration; and (b) a notification of any amendment made to the application for registration of a certification trade mark; and (c) a copy of the rules governing the use of the certification trade mark; and (d) any other document that is relevant to the application." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
