<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.34P> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "(1) Section 56 of the Act applies in relation to the Registrar’s decision on the opposition as if a reference in that section: (a) to an applicant were a reference to the holder of an IRDA; and (b) to a decision under section 55 of the Act were a reference to a decision under regulation 17A.34N. (2) If an appeal is made, the Registrar must tell the International Bureau of the decision on the appeal." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
