<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.42F> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:86e7e223760cea161330e40899bdea00c9c8345c9deccabb8a2d344cdcebc704" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.42F> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A person who made submissions to the Registrar, or was heard by the Registrar, during the course of proceedings mentioned in paragraph 17A.42C(1)(a), may appeal to the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court from a decision of the Registrar to exercise, or not exercise, a power mentioned in subregulation 17A.42A(1)." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
