<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r6.6> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "(1) For subsection 65A(4) of the Act, a person may oppose a request for amendment by filing a notice of opposition, in an approved form, within one month from the publication of the request for the amendment in a computer database maintained by the Trade Marks Office in accordance with regulation 6.3A. (2) The Registrar must give a copy of the notice to the applicant." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
